{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559528-outdated-titanic-knacks","id":1559528,"title":"Outdated titanic knacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-19T14:30:20-07:00","id":1559528,"title":"Outdated titanic knacks","content":"So, reading through Pandora's Box, I noticed a number of titanic knacks weren't in there, especially from Saints &amp; Monsters. Should I assume those are outdated/no longer used? Especially since some of them don't feel too balanced, like the Primeval immortal knack that gives a base speed scale equal to the calling rating, as well as giving access to the shockwave tag in return for 1 tension/collateral.<br /> <br /> In general, should I treat Pandora's Box as the current definite list of charms, especially for titanic knacks? Since those are a bit of a mess otherwise, with multiple full knack lists in each titan-related book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T18:16:44-07:00","id":1559529,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't treat Pandora's Box as the be all, end all of knacks and boons. Just a VERY useful tool.<br /> Truthfully I wish included some sign post citations so I can remember where the atypical Callings (such as Architect) were detailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T05:57:20-07:00","id":1559596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559528-outdated-titanic-knacks#post1559528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, reading through Pandora's Box, I noticed a number of titanic knacks weren't in there, especially from Saints &amp; Monsters. Should I assume those are outdated/no longer used? Especially since some of them don't feel too balanced, like the Primeval immortal knack that gives a base speed scale equal to the calling rating, as well as giving access to the shockwave tag in return for 1 tension/collateral.<br /> <br /> In general, should I treat Pandora's Box as the current definite list of charms, especially for titanic knacks? Since those are a bit of a mess otherwise, with multiple full knack lists in each titan-related book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Titanic Knacks, I thought it was the other way around: it's the original ones from Titanomachy which are outdated after being replaced by the list of them from Saints &amp; Monsters. And on another note, many Draconic Knacks are openly re-uses of already existing Knacks with some having updated effects, with the Dragon book explicitly saying that Scions are allowed to take these updated versions over the base ones. But that's mentioned nowhere in Pandora's Box.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559528-outdated-titanic-knacks?p=1559529#post1559529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't treat Pandora's Box as the be all, end all of knacks and boons. Just a VERY useful tool.<br /> Truthfully I wish included some sign post citations so I can remember where the atypical Callings (such as Architect) were detailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't being the be-all-end-all of player options the WHOLE POINT of Pandora's Box? And it's not the ony way it fails at being so: Innate Powers for Purviews, for exemple, aren't listed, so you still need to open up the original book the Purview was published in to know the Innate Power, which once again defeats the entire purpose of Pandora's Box of eliminating the need to sift through a half-dozen rule books and suplements at the same time to not miss anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}